\begin_layout Standard
We first consider the case of circles, i.e., 
\begin_inset Formula $d=2$
\end_inset

.
 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\OPT$
\end_inset

 be an optimal solution and 
\begin_inset Formula $\C_{\OPT}$
\end_inset

 be the circles in 
\begin_inset Formula $\OPT$
\end_inset

.
 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\eps\in(0,1/2]$
\end_inset

 be a constant and assume that 
\begin_inset Formula $1/\eps\in\mathbb{N}$
\end_inset

.
 First, we want to classify the input circles into 
\emph on
small
\emph default
 and 
\emph on
large 
\emph default
circles such that each large circle is much larger than any small circle.
 Due to the following lemma, we can do this such that we can ignore all
 circles that are neither large nor small by losing only a factor of 
\begin_inset Formula $1+\eps$
\end_inset

.
 We will use this standard shifting argument throughout the paper (see Appendix
 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:shifting"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

).
